{"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "terrace"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a flat area next to a building where people can sit and relax"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Historians wrote about these \"hanging\" gardens, which were planted on a series of terraces supported by columns by ancient Babylonians. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you write about history and civilizations."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "astonishing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "causing a feeling of great surprise or wonder "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: King Nebuchadnezzar is known to have constructed an astonishing array of  buildings."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "array"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large group or number of things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There was an array of temples, streets, palaces and walls."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to console "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to try to make someone feel less sadness or disappointment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Tradition has it that the gardens were created by the king to console his wife, who missed her homeland."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "oasis"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " an area in a desert where there is water and plants"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Although Babylon rarely received rain, the gardens were lush and provided an oasis in the desert landscape."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to irrigate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to supply something, such as land with water by using artificial means "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Even though it was an immense task given the lack of modern engines and pressure pumps in the fifth century B.C., the gardens were constantly  irrigated by using the water from the Euphrates River."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to erect"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to build something by putting together materials"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Made of bronze,the statue of the sun god Helios was erected by the citizens near the harbor of their island in about 280 B.C. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le08ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adverbial Clauses of Contrast "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">adverbial clauses </span>of contrast in your writing to express ideas or actions that are not expected. </br> Using clauses of this nature makes your writing more sophisticated and easier to read."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbial clauses</span> of contrast refer to a concession or an unexpected result of something. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The clauses are introduced by the conjunctions <span class=\"italic\">although, even though, though, whereas, despite, in spite of </span>or <span class=\"italic\">while.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Although Babylon rarely received rain</span>, the gardens were lush and provided an oasis in the desert landscape. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " These types of clauses are <span class=\"underline\">dependent</span> - meaning they cannot stand alone. They need to be attached to the main clause. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Even though</span> it was an immense task given the lack of modern engines and pressure pumps in the fifth century B.C., the gardens were constantly  irrigated by using the water from the Euphrates River."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Despite </span>being one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World, the Colossus of Rhodes is often overlooked."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">In spite of</span> its destruction, historians and tourists alike still admire this majestic work of art."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past Passive"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past </span>to talk about finished events at a particular time in the past.</br>  You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past</span> <span class=\"underline\">passive</span> when you want to focus on the action that is done to the subject. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You form the <span class=\"underline\">passive</span> by using <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">was/were</span> + past participle</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The doer or agent of the action is either not known or not mentioned as the receiver of the action is more important to the context."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:</br><span class=\"italic\">  Historians wrote about these \"hanging\" gardens, which <span class=\"strong\">were planted</span> on a series of terraces supported by columns.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes you use the preposition 'by' to mention the person or thing that did the action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:  </br><span class=\"italic\">Some believe that the gardens <span class=\"strong\">were built by</span> the King in about 600 B.C. in an area that is now southern Iraq. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The amazing \"hanging\" gardens were planted on  terraces so the vegetation spilled down."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The were built in a dry area, which made them even more wonderful to see. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Tradition has it that the gardens were created by the king to console his wife, who missed her homeland. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research ancient civilizations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use my notes to write a paragraph about an ancient wonder."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the Passive form to talk about facts and events."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to a local library and look for information about another ancient wonder."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the information from 3 different sites or books and take notes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compile the information and write a 120-150 word paragraph."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Passive form to talk about facts and events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your paragraph."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your paragraph to a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "ty