a": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn10le08ob08re7pdf01.pdf"}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "id": 11, "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Let's delve into the past. What can you learn about ancient civilizations?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}], "template_override": 1}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le08ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le08ob08re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le08ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "The city of Babylon, under King Nebuchadnezzar II, must have been a wonder to the ancient travelers' eyes. Historians wrote about these \"hanging\" gardens, which were planted on a series of terraces supported by columns by ancient Babylonians. Some believe that the gardens were built by the King in about 600 B.C. in an area that is now southern Iraq.</br>This was the height of the city's power and influence and King Nebuchadnezzar is known to have constructed an astonishing array of temples, streets, palaces and walls.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le08ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Tradition has it that the gardens were created by the king to console his wife, who missed her homeland.  Although Babylon rarely received rain, the gardens were lush and provided an oasis in the desert landscape. Even though it was an immense task given the lack of modern engines and pressure pumps in the fifth century B.C., the gardens were constantly  irrigated by using the water from the Euphrates River. It must have been an incredible site!", "id": 2, "time": "35000", "image": "engenn10le08ob08re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "Despite being one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World, the Colossus of Rhodes is often overlooked. The immense statue stood over 30 meters high, making it one of the tallest statues of the ancient world. Made of bronze, the statue of the sun god Helios was erected by the citizens near the harbor of their island in about 280 B.C.  This colossus was built as a celebration of freedom. Although the Colossus of Rhodes collapsed in an earthquake in 225 B.C.,  its fallen pieces remained in place for hundreds of years.<br/>Then, in the middle of the seventh century, the metal fragments were gathered by invading Arab tribes and were carried off. Some have noted that it took as many as 900 camels to carry the pieces away. In spite of its destruction, historians and tourists alike still admire this majestic work of art.", "id": 3, "time": "65000", "image": "engenn10le08ob08re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}, {"id": 2, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"video_src": "engenn10le08ob08re3vid01", "images": [{"text": "Great Pyramid of Giza\n</span><ul><li>Built: About 2,600 B.C.\n</li><li>Massive tombs of Egyptian pharaohs\n</li><li>Oldest of the Seven Wonders of The World\n</li><li>Is the oldest and largest of the three pyramids in the Giza pyramid complex\n</li><li>Borders what is now El Giza, Egypt\n</li><li>Consists of an estimated 2.3 million blocks\n</li><li>Was the tallest man-made structure in the world for more than 3,800 years.\n</li><li>The pyramids are the only ancient wonders still standing today.\n</li></ul>", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": ""}]}}]}]}], "type": "sena"}